' D(D2O)     ARCAB     EVAL-JUN17 Marquez Damian                   '
'                      DIST-                                       '
'----ENDF/B-VIII.beta  MATERIAL 11                                 '
'-----THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                              '
'------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               '
'                                                                  '
'******************************************************************'
'*                                                                *'
'* Temperatures = 283.6, 293.6, 300.0,                            *'
'*         323.6, 350.0, 373.6, 400.0,                            *'
'*         423.6, 450.0, 473.6, 500.0,                            *'
'*         523.6, 550.0, 573.6, 600.0 K, 623.6 K                  *'
'*                                                                *'
'* Extrapolated temperature = 650.0 K                             *'
'*                                                                *'
'* This evaluation is based on the CAB Model for heavy water[1]   *'
'* in a liquid state, T < T-crit(D2O) = 643.8 K. The file (MF7)   *'
'* was generated using NJOY 99.396[1] with a patch (upcab). One   *'
'* temperature point at 650 K was added for backward              *'
'* compatibility with ENDF/B-VII.1 scripts.                       *'
'*                                                                *'
'* The CAB model is a further development of ENDF/B-VII (2006)    *'
'* and IKE, Stuttgart (2005) models for heavy water (n + D2O);    *'
'* vibrational spectrum decomposition is applied. The continuous  *'
'* spectrum is based on MD GROMACS Calculations[2] and diffusion  *'
'* coefficients measured by Yoshida[3] and Mills[4].              *'
'*                                                                *'
'* For n + H-2-in-D2O, Skold approximation was applied for        *'
'* coherent inelastic correction with partial structure factors   *'
'* validated against experimental data measured by Soper[5].      *'
'* sig_coh(H-2)/sig_s(H-2) = 0.73194 .                            *'
'*                                                                *'
'* For oxygen in D2O, a new evaluation of the scattering kernel   *'
'* was prepared (free gas model is not applied). The scattering   *'
'* kernels for H-2-in-D2O and O-16-in-D2O were tested with        *'
'* criticality calculations in collaboration with D. Roubtsov     *'
'* from Canadian Nuclear Laboratories[6].                         *'
'*                                                                *'
'* The evaluation was prepared by:                                *'
'*                                                                *'
'* J.I. Marquez Damian, F. Cantargi, and J.R. Granada             *'
'* Nuclear Data Group - Neutron Physics Department                *'
'* Centro Atomico Bariloche - Argentina (CAB):                    *'
'*                                                                *'
'*  and                                                           *'
'*                                                                *'
'* D. Roubtsov                                                    *'
'* Canadian Nuclear Laboratories (CNL)                            *'
'* Chalk River, Canada                                            *'
'*                                                                *'
'* References:                                                    *'
'*  [1] Ann. Nucl. Energy, 65, 280 (2014)                         *'
'*      http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2013.11.014           *'
'*  [2] J. Chem. Phys. 139, 024504 (2013)                         *'
'*      http://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.4812828                       *'
'*  [3] J. Chem. Phys. 123, 164506 (2005)                         *'
'*      http://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.2056542                       *'
'*  [4] J. Phys. Chem. 77, 685 (1973)                             *'
'*      http://dx.doi.org/10.1021/j100624a025                     *'
'*  [5] Chem. Phys. 258, 121 (2000)                               *'
'*      http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/S0301-0104(00)00179-8           *'
'*  [6] Ann. Nucl. Energy, 71, 206 (2014)                         *'
'*      http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2014.03.024           *'
'*                                                                *'
'******************************************************************'
